{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017bwDfnM3xmGY6h7p6WXjqB","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md\nindex a8cdfd5b..15178854 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md\n@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@ Records and indexes written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_handoff.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_runtime_dir_test.go\n - modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n+- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n \n ### Delivery targets\n - capability:review-resume-runtime-dir-followups module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n@@ -93,7 +95,7 @@ The attempt's runtime directory is the lock: a continuation creates it, exclusiv\n \n ### Decision D2\n - Basis: R2, R3\n-The runtime directory of a continuation is named by what its predecessor recorded in `safety.runtime_id`, so a session finds the checkout where it saw it, also when an earlier engine named it at random; a round that continues its thread takes the name of the previous round's run. Only an attempt's first run derives the name from the attempt id. This answers R2 by resuming instead of refusing.\n+The runtime directory of a continuation is named by what its predecessor recorded in `safety.runtime_id`, so a session finds the checkout where it saw it, also when an earlier engine named it at random; a round that continues its thread takes the name of the previous round's run, unless that path is already there (a leftover or a live run): then the round opens a new session in its own directory, recording why, before its attempt is reserved. Only an attempt's first run derives the name from the attempt id. This answers R2 by resuming instead of refusing.\n \n ## 6. Validation\n \n@@ -107,14 +109,15 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n \n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-27: D1 in `RunReviewDispatch` (`takeContinuationRuntimeDir`) and in the plans (`awaitContinuationClaim`); D2 by `runtimeSourceOf` and `runtimeSourceAmong`; the refusal test asserts the resume's own wording (`then resume again`). `TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim`, `TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession` and `TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath` fail with each guard mutated out (the recorded name, the thread's source, the name's path, the exclusive take, the verb).\n+- 2026-11-27: review round 1 (rrn-5be6bc059866ee70) requested changes. N1: a continuation that fails before it owns its cleanup removes the directory it took (`TestRunContinuityAFailedContinuationLeavesNoRuntimeDirectory` fails with the removal mutated out). N2: a round does not continue a session whose path is held; it opens a new session with the reason, before reservation (D2). `TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread` dispatches a continued round, compares `safety.runtime_id` with the previous round's (N3, R3 end to end), and holds the path for the next round; it fails with the held-path check or the dispatch's use of the thread's name mutated out. N4 and N5 are follow-ups.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n-- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityAFailedContinuationLeavesNoRuntimeDirectory, test:TestRunContinuityTakesTheRuntimeDirectoryBeforeTheClaim, test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n - R2 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession\n-- R3 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession\n+- R3 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityRuntimeNameFollowsTheSession, test:TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread\n - R4 [satisfied] test:TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath\n \n ### Known gaps\n@@ -135,4 +138,6 @@ A continuation takes the attempt's runtime directory before its claim, and every\n L1 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-None. Origin: `pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout` (done 2026-11-26).\n+Origin: `pose-review-resume-keeps-the-sealed-checkout` (done 2026-11-26).\n+- [open] Let the wait for another resume's claim report a completed continuation as such (and to a handoff as already continued), honour cancellation, read the ledger once per poll cheaply, and turn a claim conflict after the winner finished into the recorded result (review round 1, N4). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-27)\n+- [open] Record, in the run, a continued round whose runtime name could not be read from the ledger, instead of moving its checkout silently (review round 1, N5). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-27)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\nindex a6b193df..7275c0d5 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate_rounds_test.go\n@@ -242,3 +242,28 @@ func TestReviewRoundsSurviveLossesAndResumes(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"a resumed continued round counted as cold: %s\", out)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Spec pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups R3: a round that continues\n+// its thread recreates the checkout under the previous round's runtime name;\n+// review round 1, N2: when that path is held, the round opens a new session\n+// in its own directory instead of failing after its attempt is reserved.\n+func TestReviewRoundsKeepTheCheckoutPathOfTheirThread(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := dispatchInstance(t)\n+\twriteDelegation(t, root, delegationPolicy(roundsAgent(\"rounder\", \"other\", false)))\n+\tfirst := runRecord(t, root, roundRun(t, root, \"rounder\")[\"run\"].(string))\n+\tnextReviewRound(t, root, \"fix B1\")\n+\tsecond := runRecord(t, root, roundRun(t, root, \"rounder\")[\"run\"].(string))\n+\tif second.Thread == nil || second.Thread.Mode != posemodel.ReviewThreadContinued || second.Safety == nil || first.Safety == nil || second.Safety.RuntimeID != first.Safety.RuntimeID {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a continued round moved its checkout: thread=%+v first=%v second=%v\", second.Thread, first.Safety, second.Safety)\n+\t}\n+\tnextReviewRound(t, root, \"fix B2\")\n+\theld := filepath.Join(os.TempDir(), second.Safety.RuntimeID)\n+\tif err := os.Mkdir(held, 0o700); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tdefer os.Remove(held)\n+\tthird := runRecord(t, root, roundRun(t, root, \"rounder\")[\"run\"].(string))\n+\tif third.Status != posemodel.ReviewRunCompleted || third.Thread == nil || third.Thread.Mode != posemodel.ReviewThreadNew || !strings.Contains(third.Thread.Reason, \"still in use\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a round continued into a held path: status=%s thread=%+v failure=%s\", third.Status, third.Thread, third.Failure)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\nindex 9ea10c6c..9e6e9b8f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_run_continuity_test.go\n@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ import (\n \t\"crypto/sha256\"\n \t\"encoding/hex\"\n \t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n \t\"strings\"\n@@ -350,3 +351,32 @@ func TestRunContinuityResumedReviewFindsItsSealedCheckoutAtTheSamePath(t *testin\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the resumed session did not find its checkout at %s: %d %s\", checkout, code, out)\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Review round 1 of spec pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups, N1: a\n+// continuation that fails before it owns its cleanup removes the runtime\n+// directory it took, so nothing is left for a later continuation to meet.\n+func TestRunContinuityAFailedContinuationLeavesNoRuntimeDirectory(t *testing.T) {\n+\tmarks := t.TempDir()\n+\tfirst := filepath.Join(marks, \"first\")\n+\troot, _, prior := runContinuityFixture(t, func(a *posemodel.ReviewerAdapter) {\n+\t\ta.Command = []string{\"sh\", \"-c\", `pwd > \"$1\"; printf 'session: fixture-private-session\\nreset: 2030-01-01T00:00:00Z\\ndecision: rejected\\n'; exit 75`, \"sh\", first}\n+\t})\n+\traw, err := os.ReadFile(first)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\truntimeDir := filepath.Dir(strings.TrimSpace(string(raw)))\n+\tstore := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n+\tplan, err := store.PlanReviewResume(prior.RunID)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tplan.OnStart = func(string) error { return errors.New(\"no hand-back here\") }\n+\trun, _ := store.RunReviewDispatch(plan, time.Now)\n+\tif run.Status != posemodel.ReviewRunFailed {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a failing hand-back did not fail the continuation: %+v\", run.Status)\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := os.Lstat(runtimeDir); !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a failed continuation left its runtime directory %s: %v\", runtimeDir, err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\nindex 6f59ccbc..a4a4a19d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n@@ -661,6 +661,8 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t}\n \trun.Safety = safety\n \tvar cleanup func() error\n+\t// The runtime directory a continuation took before its claim.\n+\tpreparedRuntimeDir := \"\"\n \tvar cleanupErr error\n \tvar terminationFailed bool\n \tcleaned := false\n@@ -693,6 +695,12 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t}()\n \ttranscript := []byte{}\n \tfinish := func(status, failure string) (ReviewRun, error) {\n+\t\tif cleanup == nil && preparedRuntimeDir != \"\" {\n+\t\t\t// The continuation took its directory before the claim and fails\n+\t\t\t// before it owns its cleanup: nothing is in it yet (review round\n+\t\t\t// 1, N1).\n+\t\t\t_ = os.Remove(preparedRuntimeDir)\n+\t\t}\n \t\tdoCleanup()\n \t\tif cancelled != nil && cancelled.Load() && status != ReviewRunCompleted {\n \t\t\t// A deliberate cancellation is a failure, never a resumable interruption,\n@@ -713,7 +721,6 @@ func (s Store) RunReviewDispatchContext(parent context.Context, plan DispatchPla\n \t\treturn finish(ReviewRunFailed, \"the run was not started: \"+err.Error())\n \t}\n \tvar attempt DelegatedReviewAttempt\n-\tpreparedRuntimeDir := \"\"\n \tif plan.predecessor == nil {\n \t\tvar err error\n \t\tattempt, err = s.prepareDelegatedReviewAttempt(plan, now())\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\nindex 3e3d64db..ebafd568 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ import (\n \t\"encoding/json\"\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"io\"\n+\t\"os\"\n \t\"reflect\"\n \t\"regexp\"\n \t\"sort\"\n@@ -690,6 +691,13 @@ func (s Store) planReviewThread(plan *DispatchPlan) error {\n \t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous round's session cannot be resumed: it recorded no session or the agent declares no resume\"\n \tcase failed != nil:\n \t\tthread.Reason = FailedContinuationReason(failed)\n+\tcase previousRoundCheckoutHeld(*prior):\n+\t\t// The continued session would work where the previous round's run\n+\t\t// did; that path is held by a leftover or a live run, so the round\n+\t\t// opens a new session in its own directory instead of failing after\n+\t\t// its attempt is reserved (spec pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups,\n+\t\t// review round 1, N2).\n+\t\tthread.Reason = \"the previous 