{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UkLm3Nx9mXmuxTajHXh6PS","type":"tool_result","content":".pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:148:- Amend `round-protocol` R6: the default is `continue-thread` — a round after\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:151:  Open a new session, with the reason recorded, on a vendor change, a broken\n.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:203:4. **Rounds:** `continue-thread` is the default, accepting the anchoring risk\n.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:6:A review round whose attempt failed while continuing a session opens a new session on its next attempt, with the reason recorded, instead of resuming the same dead session.\n.pose/changelogs/unreleased/pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n.pose/roadmaps/delegation.md:85:**Exit gate:** with `continue-thread`, the round after a rejection resumes the\n.pose/roadmaps/delegation.md:87:to continue or the round threshold opens a new session with the reason recorded; prior\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:46:- R6: When `routing.rounds` is `continue-thread` (the default), a round after the first shall resume the thread's current session; it shall open a new session, recording the reason, when the agent's vendor changes, the supersession chain is broken, the session can no longer be resumed, or the scope reaches the round threshold. When `routing.rounds` is `cold-session`, every round shall open a new session. The run shall record the session lineage and `pose review verify` shall disclose it.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:109:Brief gains a prior-findings section; the draft gains `prior_findings` and `sweep`; `delegation.json` gains `routing.rounds` (`continue-thread` or `cold-session`) and a round threshold.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:116:- [x] Thread session continuation, forced new sessions and lineage\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:125:- Minimal option: a new session for every round\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:126:- Selected option: continue the thread's session by default (`continue-thread`), with `cold-session` available by policy and a new session forced on a vendor change, a broken chain, an unresumable session or the round threshold\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:150:[Omitted long matching line]\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:158:- Selected option: continue the session the previous round's concluding run ended with only when the same agent runs the next round; another agent of the same vendor opens a new session, as a vendor change, a broken chain, an unresumable session and the threshold do. The threshold applies from the round that reaches it (`routing.round_threshold`, 5 by default). After a handoff the session the handoff run captured is the one a later round continues, which delivers R10 of `pose-delegation-handoff`\n.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md:167:[Omitted long matching line]\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:21:A review round whose attempt failed while continuing a session opens a new session on its next attempt, with the reason recorded, and the gates of the delegation roadmaps say what was delivered.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:30:- The new session gets the full brief, so no prior finding is lost.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:43:- R1: When a round's run that continued a session has failed for the same bundle, the next attempt shall open a new session and record why, naming the run that failed.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:57:- A continuation that fails then opens a new session instead of failing again.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:86:- [x] Open a new session after a failed continuation\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:95:- Selected option: any continuation that failed gives way to a new session on the next attempt\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:116:- R1 [satisfied] capability:delegated-review-expired-session evidence:integration check:delegated-review-expired-session-integration test:TestFailedContinuationOpensANewSession test:TestFailedContinuationReasonIsBounded report:.pose/results/delivery-validation.json commit:c5eb59617874007d4b0dcbd337288ffa12176fb0 — The next attempt after a failed continuation opens a new session and names the run.\n.pose/specs/2026-10-31-pose-delegated-review-expired-session.md:124:A review attempt that failed while continuing a session gives way to a new session on the next attempt, with the reason recorded and no vendor text parsed. The gates of `dispatch`, `surface`, `rounds` and `retirement` now state what was delivered. Independently reviewed by Codex in one round, by the reviewer who found the gaps.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md:98:[Omitted long matching line]\n.pose/specs/2026-11-26-pose-review-resume-runtime-dir-followups.md:112:[Omitted long matching line]\nPOSE.md:956:[Omitted long matching line]\nlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md:951:[Omitted long matching line]\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:943:[Omitted long matching line]\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:951:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"08d130b2-20c9-4cea-abfd-b1c6e62dc622","timestamp":"2026-11-27T09:02:20.689Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":".pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md:148:- Amend `round-prot